WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:03.580
Crowd: GOOD MORNING, JOHN!!!!

00:00:03.580 --> 00:00:05.820
Hank: Theoretically, a bunch of people just said good morning to you,

00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:07.140
but that has not happened to me yet,

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:09.340
because it is five in the morning,

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:12.300
and I have to get on a plane....

00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:14.040
There was a guy....that whole time I was talking....

00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:15.220
he was very quiet.

00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:19.460
Did you know, John, that planes have a kind of a butt hole?

00:00:19.460 --> 00:00:22.200
The majority of the exhaust on a plane comes out through the engines,

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:25.160
but there is also a thing called the auxiliary power unit,

00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:27.440
which powers all of the electronics on the plane

00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:32.680
like everything from the crackling speakers to the hydraulics to the vacuum-powered poop pump thingy

00:00:32.860 --> 00:00:37.420
and it vents out its exhaust through a port that is called, in my head,

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:38.480
the planus.

00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:40.880
That was the punchline.  That's why I told the whole story.

00:00:41.420 --> 00:00:43.260
Yep.  It's all true, though.

00:00:43.260 --> 00:00:45.340
Is it weird that Jean Luc Picard doesn't have hair?

00:00:45.340 --> 00:00:47.420
Shouldn't they have cured balding by the 24th century?

00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:50.580
Did you know....that fish don't fart?

00:00:50.580 --> 00:00:55.160
This is...this might not sound that weird, but it's actually really weird.

00:00:55.160 --> 00:00:58.660
There are some fish that use gas internally as ballast...

00:00:58.660 --> 00:01:00.180
most of them burp that up,

00:01:00.180 --> 00:01:02.360
uh, when they need to get rid of some air, but

00:01:02.360 --> 00:01:05.040
some of them do...have it come out the other end.

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:08.900
But as far as, like, bacterial gas produced in the gut of fish,

00:01:08.900 --> 00:01:11.200
it doesn't come out of them.  It is produced though

00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:15.340
cause they have the same kind of gas producing organisms in their gut that we do.

00:01:15.700 --> 00:01:18.260
It is a mystery...where that gas goes!

00:01:18.260 --> 00:01:20.560
That's a weird thing for us to not know!

00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:25.720
(sleepily) In addition to being exhausted, I'm also bursting with excitement internally...

00:01:25.720 --> 00:01:28.500
*music in background* Super.....that's quite a dance song....

00:01:28.780 --> 00:01:30.700
Really just, uh, quite happy

00:01:30.700 --> 00:01:34.780
that, uh, at least 55% of the Supreme Court of the United States,

00:01:35.640 --> 00:01:36.760
uh, is not crazy!

00:01:36.760 --> 00:01:39.400
It's nice to see that Canadian currency has made a bit of a come back

00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:41.960
and the only difference between it and American currency now apparently

00:01:42.700 --> 00:01:47.560
is that Canadians realize that 30 bucks and 29.95 are the same freakin' thing.

00:01:47.560 --> 00:01:51.340
Eeeehhh and whenever you're going to Portland, everybody always says,

00:01:51.340 --> 00:01:52.860
"Don't forget your Wii!"

00:01:52.860 --> 00:01:54.200
Been dropped off at a loading dock

00:01:54.440 --> 00:01:56.200
I don't know what I'm doing

00:01:56.480 --> 00:01:58.560
or....what...I should do now.

00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:00.740
I think I just met someone who's even more tired than me!

00:02:01.620 --> 00:02:02.900
It's Devon Murray!

00:02:02.900 --> 00:02:03.740
Devon: "Hey, how's it going?"

00:02:03.740 --> 00:02:04.540
Hank: "How are you doin'?

00:02:04.540 --> 00:02:08.260
Devon: "Not too badly...a little bit worse for wear with all the flyin' but then again there..."

00:02:08.260 --> 00:02:10.940
Hank: "This is a terrible thing to say, but I keep expecting him to light something on fire."

00:02:10.940 --> 00:02:12.620
Hank:"Tell me the story that you just told me."

00:02:12.620 --> 00:02:15.040
Devon: "I just blew my microwave up the other day...

00:02:15.040 --> 00:02:19.800
I was, eh, upstairs - and all of a sudden - havin' a shower, I come back downstairs.  There's smoke all over the house.

00:02:19.800 --> 00:02:20.900
It was only a brand new microwave.

00:02:20.900 --> 00:02:23.400
So..first time being used I should have watched it.

00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:24.220
Hank: "That doesn't sound like it was your fault."

00:02:24.220 --> 00:02:25.700
Devon: "Oh no, of course it wasn't."

00:02:25.700 --> 00:02:26.200
Hank: "Okay."

00:02:26.480 --> 00:02:29.440
Devon: "But still...hashtag, eh, Seamus."

00:02:29.440 --> 00:02:30.500
*Hank laughs*
Devon: "That's it."

00:02:31.520 --> 00:02:32.880
*chorus of hello's*

00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:37.220
Hank: "So it turns out that the cast of the Lizzie Bennett Diaries just breaks out into song pretty frequently."

00:02:37.220 --> 00:02:38.780
(person 1 singing) Portland...

00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:41.800
(person 2 singing)...watcha doin' Portland?

00:02:41.840 --> 00:02:45.060
(person 1 singing) So many people I never knew in Portland.

00:02:45.060 --> 00:02:46.480
(person 2 singing) .....portland...

00:02:46.480 --> 00:02:48.900
I'm about to go on stage with Lauren Fairweather

00:02:48.900 --> 00:02:50.720
wearing my Lauren Fairweather shirt.

00:02:51.280 --> 00:02:53.200
Insert crowd screaming now!

00:02:53.280 --> 00:02:56.300
*crowd screaming*

00:02:56.300 --> 00:02:59.400
That's why I'm happy to get up early in the morning to do this kind of stuff

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:02.300
because that is better than any amount of sleep possible.

00:03:02.300 --> 00:03:03.120
John -

00:03:03.220 --> 00:03:06.200
Crowd: " - I'll see you on Tuesday!"

00:03:06.520 --> 00:03:09.160
But of course I was wrong when I said that

00:03:09.320 --> 00:03:11.080
I won't see John on Tuesday

00:03:11.080 --> 00:03:12.740
I will see Rosie on Tuesday.

00:03:13.280 --> 00:03:14.320
I am very tired.

00:03:14.600 --> 00:03:15.960
I am going....to go.

00:03:17.080 --> 00:03:17.580
To bed.

00:03:18.640 --> 00:03:20.680
Yay pillowwssss!

00:03:21.140 --> 00:03:23.220
I'm so happy about this bed!!

